# 25. QUESTIONS ABOUT SECURITY

### "Why isn't HTTPS enough?"

Because HTTPS protects communication in transit but does not automatically prevent:

- SQL injection
- XSS
- Broken access control
- CSRF
- Business logic flaws
- Vulnerable server software

---

### "Why isn't a firewall enough?"

Because attackers may exploit:

- Allowed traffic
- Compromised credentials
- Application vulnerabilities
- Insider access
- Misconfigurations

Defense requires multiple layers.

